, system disk, data disk, GPU, network card, power supply, driver version, and Cuda version.","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_2de074594217","citation_index":36,"eligibility_reason":"The focused question explicitly requests detailed hardware and software configurations (host name, IP, OS, CPU, etc.). This statement correctly identifies the specific requirements of the focused question.","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}},{"claim_ref":"claim:e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57:01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab:claim_2807c04f4742","tool_call_id":"01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab","tool_name":"document_inspect","source_event_sequence":20,"status":"verified","claim":"The provided page (page 2) contains sections for 'VPN Login Information', 'After-sales Support', and 'Precautions'.","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_2807c04f4742","citation_index":37,"eligibility_reason":"The image clearly displays three main sections with headers: 'VPN 登录信息' (VPN Login Information), '售后支持' (After-sales Support), and '注意事项' (Precautions).","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}},{"claim_ref":"claim:e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57:01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab:claim_d6554cde027c","tool_call_id":"01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab","tool_name":"document_inspect","source_event_sequence":20,"status":"verified","claim":"The 'VPN Login Information' section lists the client (forticlient), gateway (61.49.53.8), custom port (60443), and username (xinsi).","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_d6554cde027c","citation_index":38,"eligibility_reason":"The 'VPN 登录信息' table in the image contains rows for Client ('forticlient'), Gateway ('61.49.53.8'), Custom Port ('60443'), and Username ('xinsi'). The description matches the visual data perfectly.","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}},{"claim_ref":"claim:e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57:01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab:claim_191f64ea1afb","tool_call_id":"01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab","tool_name":"document_inspect","source_event_sequence":20,"status":"verified","claim":"The 'After-sales Support' section lists the customer service center (Century Huateng Customer Service Center), email (cc@neolink.com), phone (4006519966), sales contact (Zhao Hanlun), and customer service contact (Not filled).","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_191f64ea1afb","citation_index":39,"eligibility_reason":"The '售后支持' table lists Customer Service Center as '世纪互联客户服务中心', Email as 'cc@neolink.com', Phone as '4006519966', Sales as '赵翰伦', and Customer Service as '未填写'. All details match the image.","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}},{"claim_ref":"claim:e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57:01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab:claim_ef97e3c13050","tool_call_id":"01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab","tool_name":"document_inspect","source_event_sequence":20,"status":"verified","claim":"The 'Precautions' section mentions that the test resource starts counting from 0:00 on August 30, 2025, and will expire at 0:00 on September 2, 2025.","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_ef97e3c13050","citation_index":40,"eligibility_reason":"Item 4 under '注意事项' states that the test resource starts counting from August 30, 2025, at 0:00 and expires on September 2, 2025, at 0:00. This matches the text in the image exactly.","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}},{"claim_ref":"claim:e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57:01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab:claim_56c3f5cfdc03","tool_call_id":"01a0bc69-d8ac-7b33-a992-ab7f2626ffab","tool_name":"document_inspect","source_event_sequence":20,"status":"verified","claim":"The page does not contain the specific hardware and software configuration details requested in the focused question, such as host name, internal IP, operating system, CPU, memory, system disk, data disk, GPU, network card, power supply, driver version, or Cuda version.","source":{"type":"image","library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","timestamp_start":null,"timestamp_end":null,"uri":"/media/libraries/default/assets/2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d/document/pages/1.png","metadata":{"asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d"}},"supports":[],"modalities":["image"],"sampling_range":null,"claim_id":"claim_56c3f5cfdc03","citation_index":41,"eligibility_reason":"A review of the entire page confirms that it only contains VPN login credentials, support contacts, and usage precautions. It does not contain any tables or text listing server specifications like Host Name, Internal IP, CPU, Memory, Disk, GPU, or Driver versions.","locator":{"library_id":"default","asset_id":"2af90f93-aff5-463b-8ab6-1ea20710224d","modality":"image","evidence_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","segment_id":"chunk-c2c680720c4df314f87dcaae42fd4496","time_range":null}}]},"config":{"enabled":true,"gate_enabled":true,"targeted_repair_enabled":false,"pass_threshold":75,"max_retries":0,"allow_low_confidence_output":true,"timeout_seconds":20.0},"reviewer_model":"vllm/Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8"}}}

event: message_delta
data: {"type":"message_delta","run_id":"e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57","sequence":26,"created_at":"2026-09-20T01:24:40.230877Z","payload":{"text":"答案：该资源交付通知书向上海唯纳新思智能科技有限公司交付了一台配置为Intel 8480+ ×2 CPU、64GB DDR5 ×32内存、8块Nvidia v8cM450 HGX GPU、960G SATA SSD系统盘×2及3.84T NVME SSD数据盘×8的高性能计算主机[1]。交付资源还包括400G NDR Infiniband、200G HDR Infiniband及25G双端口网卡等多网络配置，运行Ubuntu 22.04系统并预装CUDA 12.5及驱动版本550.90.07[2]。"}}

event: message_completed
data: {"type":"message_completed","run_id":"e42466f1-e3a2-44b3-8d91-c3815ba4ff57","sequence":27,"created_at":"2026-09-20T01:24:40.233816Z","payload":{"text":"答案：该资源交付通知书向上海唯纳新思智能科技有限公司交付了一台配置为Intel 8480+ ×2 CPU、64GB DDR5 ×32内存、8块Nvidia v8cM450 HGX GPU、960G SATA SSD系统盘×2及3.84T NVME SSD数据盘×8的高性能计算主机[1]。交付资源还包括400G NDR Infiniband、200G HDR Infiniband及25G双端口网卡等多网络配置，运行Ubuntu 22.04系统并预装CUDA 12.5及驱动版本550.90.07[2]。","raw_model_output":"{\"truncated\": true, \"char_limit\": 50000, \"payload_prefix\": \"{\\\"messages\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"user_query:\\\\n根据知识库中上海唯纳新思资源交付通知书 PDF，用两句话概括交付内容，答案里必须带方括号数字引用如[1]。\\\\n\\\\n## Skill Reminder\\\\n\\\\nProject Skill Reminder. This project ships ViKnow skills that encode\\\\nworkflow order, evidence rules, and tool-use conventions. If a skill\\\\nmatches, invoke it before calling workflow tools.\\\\n\\\\nSkill: knowledge-qa-v2. Invoke when: answering questions about configured knowledge-base content, manuals, SOPs, product notes, training material, videos, documents, whether the knowledge base contains something, what documents/devices are available, or any request that might use knowledge, search, inspect, or evidence tools.\\\\nSkill file: /workspace/.skills/knowledge-qa-v2/SKILL.md\\\\n\\\\nSkill: visual-ground. Invoke when: Use when the user asks WHERE something is in an image or selected video frame (\\\\\\\"哪里有X\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"X在哪里\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"找到X\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"图中X的位置\\\\\\\"), or HOW MANY physical targets are simultaneously visible in one image/frame (\\\\\\\"图中有几个X\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"count the visible X\\\\\\\"). Do not use it for OCR/text occurrences, repeated actions, durations, or categories accumulated across a video. Call visual_ground with query as a COMPLETE NATURAL-LANGUAGE QUESTION that QUALIFIES the target (e.g. \\\\\\\"图中切好的完整黄色柠檬片有几片？\\\\\\\"), never a bare noun like \\\\\\\"柠檬片\\\\\\\". For video counts, pick the frame AFTER the action finishes, then count with visual_ground; its detection count is authoritative.\\\\nSkill file: /workspace/.skills/visual-ground/SKILL.md\\\\n\\\\nRules: For matching requests, the first tool call must be read_file on\\\\nthe exact skill file path listed above for the matching skill.\\\\nNever glob, ls, or search the filesystem for SKILL.md or skill\\\\ndirectories; the paths above are final and already staged.\\\\nDo not call knowledge, search, inspect, or evidence tools before\\\\nreading the skill. Do not execute workflow steps from memory.\\\", \\\"additional_kwargs\\\": {}, \\\"response_metadata\\\": {}, \\\"type\\\": \\\"human\\\", \\\"name\\\": null, \\\"id\\\": \\\"518bf1e8-f154-46b3-a016-02a9f4054b16\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"additional_kwargs\\\": {}, \\\"response_metadata\\\": {\\\"finish_reason\\\": \\\"tool_calls\\\", \\\"model_name\\\": \\\"viknow-agent-chat\\\", \\\"model_provider\\\": \\\"openai\\\"}, \\\"type\\\": \\\"ai\\\", \\\"name\\\": null, \\\"id\\\": \\\"lc_run--01a0bc69-7e64-7752-a8bb-69f75070ceb7\\\", \\\"tool_calls\\\": [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"file_path\\\": \\\"/workspace/.skills/knowledge-qa-v2/SKILL.md\\\", \\\"limit\\\": 1000}, \\\"id\\\": \\\"chatcmpl-tool-bce25656b6cae8c4\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"tool_call\\\"}], \\\"invalid_tool_calls\\\": [], \\\"usage_metadata\\\": {\\\"input_tokens\\\": 12194, \\\"output_tokens\\\": 53, \\\"total_tokens\\\": 12247, \\\"input_token_details\\\": {}, \\\"output_token_details\\\": {\\\"reasoning\\\": 0}}}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"     1\\\\t---\\\\n     2\\\\tname: knowledge-qa-v2\\\\n     3\\\\tdescription: 'answering questions about configured knowledge-base content, manuals,\\\\n     4\\\\t  SOPs, product notes, training material, videos, documents, whether the knowledge\\\\n     5\\\\t  base contains something, what documents/devices are available, or any request that\\\\n     6\\\\t  might use knowledge, search, inspect, or evidence tools.\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\t  '\\\\n     9\\\\tmetadata:\\\\n    10\\\\t  version: 0.27.4\\\\n    11\\\\t---\\\\n    12\\\\t# ViKnow Knowledge QA v2\\\\n    13\\\\t\\\\n    14\\\\tUse this skill for knowledge-base questions requiring search, inspection, or\\\\n    15\\\\tevidence tools. Do not use it for general everyday questions.\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\n    17\\\\t## Non-Negotiables\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\n    19\\\\t- Search results are candidates only. Do not answer from raw `knowledge_search`\\\\n    20\\\\t  text, indexed transcripts, indexed visible-text snippets, captions, or\\\\n    21\\\\t  `list_video_segments`.\\\\n    22\\\\t- Final factual claims must come from current-run inspect `claims` or valid\\\\n    23\\\\t  historical verified claims.\\\\n    24\\\\t- Discard failed tool results and claims with `confidence <= 0`. For\\\\n    25\\\\t  `document_inspect`, only use claims returned by the tool.\\\\n    26\\\\t- When the user has not fixed the scope, use `knowledge_discover`. Select a clear\\\\n    27\\\\t  best match yourself; if multiple plausible sources would materially change the\\\\n    28\\\\t  answer, state the ambiguity and ask the user to confirm the intended source.\\\\n    29\\\\t- If evidence is partial, ambiguous, or conflicting, say so instead of filling\\\\n    30\\\\t  gaps from general knowledge.\\\\n    31\\\\t- A verified claim whose category, section or other scope is narrower than the\\\\n    32\\\\t  original question does not complete that question. Before answering, inspect\\\\n    33\\\\t  another returned candidate when its search text reports the same requested\\\\n    34\\\\t  metric and period under a different explicit scope or value. This selects\\\\n    35\\\\t  materially different candidates; it does not require inspecting every hit.\\\\n    36\\\\t- When verified same-period, same-unit values are non-overlapping components\\\\n    37\\\\t  that together cover an unqualified requested metric, answer with their sum and\\\\n    38\\\\t  show each input. Otherwise report the values by scope.\\\\n    39\\\\t- **Visible-object counts and locations require `visual_ground`.** For an\\\\n    40\\\\t  answer slot about the count or location of targets visible in a selected image\\\\n    41\\\\t  or video, read the `visual-ground` skill before calling that tool and base the\\\\n    42\\\\t  final slot on its eligible claim. Do not force document, transcript, table,\\\\n    43\\\\t  duration, or other non-visual quantities through `visual_ground`.\\\\n    44\\\\t\\\\n    45\\\\t## Direct Answer Contract\\\\n    46\\\\t\\\\n    47\\\\tBegin the final answer with `Answer:` or `答案：`, immediately followed by the\\\\n    48\\\\trequested fact, final calculation result and unit, requested enumeration items,\\\\n    49\\\\tor what cannot be determined. Add applicable citations there. Only afterward give\\\\n    50\\\\tsources, arithmetic, details, or limitations. Never expose internal process.\\\\n    51\\\\t\\\\n    52\\\\t## Tool Contract\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\n    54\\\\t- Keep the user's explicit source constraints; treat sources you select as\\\\n    55\\\\t  hypotheses until their identity and relevance are established. A topic match\\\\n    56\\\\t  does not establish that a library contains a named document. If results do\\\\n    57\\\\t  not address the requested source, reassess your selection and use discovery\\\\n    58\\\\t  to locate it. Changing a candidate source does not change the user's target.\\\\n    59\\\\t- `list_video_segments` and `list_doc_segments` are bounded locator catalogs.\\\\n    60\\\\t  For ordinary QA, call them with `mode=select` and one focused subquestion;\\\\n    61\\\\t  their output is never answer evidence. Use `video_inspect_2_0` or `document_inspect`\\\\n    62\\\\t  on selected locators before citing a fact.\\\\n    63\\\\t- Once a selected library contains the named target or topic, keep retrieval in that\\\\n    64\\\\t  library. Repeated search misses do not justify switching libraries; switch only\\\\n    65\\\\t  when discovery shows the target is absent or the user explicitly requests\\\\n    66\\\\t  cross-library coverage.\\\\n    67\\\\t- `knowledge_search` returns candidates, not answer evidence. Inspect a plausible,\\\\n    68\\\\t  inspectable candidate before broadening retrieval.\\\\n    69\\\\t- Inspect calls must copy identity and boundary fields from one selected candidate.\\\\n    70\\\\t  Only eligible inspect claims can support final factual claims.\\\\n    71\\\\t\\\\n    72\\\\t## ViKnow Expert Model\\\\n    73\\\\tRuntime may provide `ViKnow 专家大模型` before planning. Use it for terms, entities, relationships, professional background, and query planning. For conceptual or entity-relationship answers, it may support final claims; state that the answer is according to ViKnow expert model. Do not use it to replace retrieval and inspection for specific documents, videos, SOPs, parameter sources, timestamps, or indexed-content existence. Current-run inspect claims override ViKnow expert model on conflict.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\t## Reasoning Phases\\\\n    76\\\\t\\\\n    77\\\\tThese phases are not a fixed pipeline. Use only the phases needed for the\\\\n    78\\\\tcurrent question, but obey the tool ordering rules below.\\\\n    79\\\\t\\\\n    80\\\\t### Phase 1: Grounding Setup\\\\n    81\\\\t\\\\n    82\\\\tDecide whether the answer needs a knowledge base, a user-uploaded image, or\\\\n    83\\\\tboth.\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\tCall `knowledge_discover` unless an explicit library is already supplied or the\\\\n    86\\\\tquestion is clearly image-only. Pick the most relevant library.\\\\n    87\\\\t\\\\n    88\\\\tUse `uploaded_image_search` only for a user-uploaded workspace image. If the\\\\n    89\\\\tcurrent workspace includes a user-uploaded image and the image may affect the\\\\n    90\\\\tanswer, call `uploaded_image_search` before `query_refine`, `knowledge_search`,\\\\n    91\\\\tor any inspect tool. This includes direct image understanding intents: visible\\\\n    92\\\\ttext reading, counting visible items, object identification, scene description,\\\\n    93\\\\tscreenshots, charts, labels, interfaces, and photos. Do not answer directly\\\\n    94\\\\tfrom model visual perception or `read_file` for these uploaded image questions.\\\\n    95\\\\t\\\\n    96\\\\tIf the uploaded image may affect a knowledge-base answer, call\\\\n    97\\\\t`knowledge_discover` first, wait for its result, then call\\\\n    98\\\\t`uploaded_image_search`. Pass the uploaded image `workspace_path`, the original\\\\n    99\\\\tuser `query`, and the selected `library_id` when a relevant library was found.\\\\n   100\\\\tOmit `library_id` only when `knowledge_discover` found no relevant library, an\\\\n   101\\\\texplicit library is unavailable, or the question is clearly image-only. Do not\\\\n   102\\\\tguess image contents yourself.\\\\n   103\\\\t\\\\n   104\\\\tUse the `uploaded_image_search.decision` value to choose the next phase:\\\\n   105\\\\t\\\\n   106\\\\t- `answer_from_image`: answer from the uploaded image result. Only use\\\\n   107\\\\t  `answer_from_image` as a final answer when the user asks solely for visible\\\\n   108\\\\t  image content and not for knowledge-base, procedure, video, or indexed\\\\n   109\\\\t  material context.\\\\n   110\\\\t- `search_knowledge`: continue to query planning or retrieval.\\\\n   111\\\\t- `mismatch`: explain that the uploaded image does not match the query or\\\\n   112\\\\t  selected knowledge scope, then ask the user for a relevant image or more\\\\n   113\\\\t  context. After `mismatch`, do not call `knowledge_search`.\\\\n   114\\\\t- `cannot_process_image`: explain the image processing issue and ask for a\\\\n   115\\\\t  better image or clarification.\\\\n   116\\\\t\\\\n   117\\\\t### Phase 2: Query Planning\\\\n   118\\\\t\\\\n   119\\\\tA new run starts with its current user input as slot `answer`, even for a follow-up.\\\\n   120\\\\tUse conversation history to interpret references to earlier turns, then revise\\\\n   121\\\\tthis run's goals when needed. Do not treat an earlier run's plan as this run's\\\\n   122\\\\tcompletion target. `answer_plan(action=\\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\")` restarts the current run's plan.\\\\n   123\\\\tKeep a direct question short; split goals as independent evidence needs appear.\\\\n   124\\\\t\\\\n   125\\\\tGive each slot a required evidence scope from its fact type and requested\\\\n   126\\\\tsource. A requested source is part of the fact. Evidence from one source may\\\\n   127\\\\tsupport a separate answer slot, but it does not verify a slot scoped to what\\\\n   128\\\\tanother source shows. Use separate answer slots to compare observed behavior\\\\n   129\\\\tand written requirements.\\\\n   130\\\\t\\\\n   131\\\\t`query_refine` returns suggestions, not the current plan. Pass the original\\\\n   132\\\\tquestion unchanged and put additional context in context fields. Use it when\\\\n   133\\\\tindependent facts, ambiguity or a new direction need planning; precise questions\\\\n   134\\\\tmay keep the initial slot. Adopt or revise suggestions with `answer_plan(action=update)`.\\\\n   135\\\\tYou can revise goals without calling query_refine again.\\\\n   136\\\\t\\\\n   137\\\\tUse view for current goals and evidence. Record candidates separately from verified\\\\n   138\\\\tclaims; not_found requires exhausted planned retrieval and plausible candidates.\\\\n   139\\\\tUse goal context for interpretations, notes for supporting/conflicting observations,\\\\n   140\\\\tgaps and next checks, and rationale for changes. Preserve the user's requirements\\\\n   141\\\\teven when evidence answers a different question. A supported answer needs no invented doubt.\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\tBefore splitting, replacing or removing goals with `update.slot_definitions`, binding\\\\n   144\\\\ta retrieval batch, or repairing plan payloads, read `references/answer-plan.md`.\\\\n   145\\\\tThe plan is investigation state, not evidence; historical, expert-model and\\\\n   146\\\\timage-only answer paths do not require fabricated current-run claims to close a goal.\\\\n   147\\\\t\\\\n   148\\\\t### Phase 3: Retrieval\\\\n   149\\\\t\\\\n   150\\\\tFind candidate evidence.\\\\n   151\\\\t\\\\n   152\\\\tFor an initial focused search, prefer `top_k=5`; 3–5 is a useful starting range,\\\\n   153\\\\tnot a fixed limit. It caps the final evidence count, not internal retrieval.\\\\n   154\\\\tIf relevant results leave a coverage gap, a larger window such as 10 may help.\\\\n   155\\\\tIf results are off-target or repetitive, revise the subquery instead of merely\\\\n   156\\\\trequesting more of the same. Top K results alone cannot establish exhaustive coverage.\\\\n   157\\\\t\\\\n   158\\\\tChoose queries by uncovered slots; skip goals already verified.\\\\n   159\\\\tAn adopted batch may be recorded with answer_plan; read `references/answer-plan.md`\\\\n   160\\\\tfor bindings, progress updates and goal revision. Do not rerun a search merely to attach it.\\\\n   161\\\\tCoverage records your current assessment, not a mandatory full-document traversal.\\\\n   162\\\\t\\\\n   163\\\\tWithin one library, do not repeat an already successful normalized query with an\\\\n   164\\\\tequal or narrower result window. Reuse its candidates; increase `top_k` only when\\\\n   165\\\\tthe existing window cannot cover an unresolved slot. The same query may run in\\\\n   166\\\\tanother in-scope library. Skip planned queries whose slots are already verified.\\\\n   167\\\\t\\\\n   168\\\\tWithin a batch, collect candidates for the uncovered slots, then inspect or\\\\n   169\\\\treject plausible candidates. Do not conclude that evidence is absent while a\\\\n   170\\\\treasonable untried query still serves an uncovered slot. Review slot coverage\\\\n   171\\\\tbefore deciding whether to refine the plan or stop retrieval.\\\\n   172\\\\t\\\\n   173\\\\tAfter the first eligible claim, compare the remaining candidates with both the\\\\n   174\\\\toriginal question and that claim. Keep a candidate when it may add another part\\\\n   175\\\\tof the requested quantity, establish a different supported scope, contradict the\\\\n   176\\\\tclaim, or otherwise change the conclusion. Reject candidates that are clearly\\\\n   177\\\\toff-scope or repeat the same fact at the same boundary. This comparison selects\\\\n   178\\\\tthe next useful inspection; it does not make every search hit mandatory.\\\\n   179\\\\tFor a direct-fact question, stop expanding when one claim directly covers the\\\\n   180\\\\trequested subject, predicate, period and scope. A related fact about a different\\\\n   181\\\\tpredicate is not another answer. Continue across sections when the verified claim\\\\n   182\\\\tis explicitly narrower than an unqualified quantity in the original question,\\\\n   183\\\\tor when the question requests a list, comparison or total.\\\\n   184\\\\t\\\\n   185\\\\tFor each uncovered answer slot, classify relevant candidates as:\\\\n   186\\\\t\\\\n   187\\\\t- `keep_for_inspect`: plausibly covers the slot and has an inspectable evidence\\\\n   188\\\\t  boundary;\\\\n   189\\\\t- `reject_with_reason`: does not cover the slot, lacks the evidence modality\\\\n   190\\\\t  needed for the fact, or duplicates a stronger candidate;\\\\n   191\\\\t- `need_more_locator`: may cover the slot but lacks a reliable inspectable\\\\n   192\\\\t  boundary or sufficient coverage.\\\\n   193\\\\t\\\\n   194\\\\tInspect kept candidates before broadening beyond the current exploration batch.\\\\n   195\\\\tWhen selection is ambiguous, spans modalities, or needs coverage expansion, read\\\\n   196\\\\t`references/evidence-candidate-audit.md` before proceeding.\\\\n   197\\\\t\\\\n   198\\\\tUse `list_video_segments` only when no kept search candidate can resolve the\\\\n   199\\\\tvideo coverage gap, the user asks about a whole video, or temporal coverage\\\\n   200\\\\tneeds expansion. Start with action, object, or state terms from the uncovered\\\\n   201\\\\tslot, refine the query before widening coverage, then call it with `mode=select`.\\\\n   202\\\\tDo not request a whole catalog in ordinary QA. Read\\\\n   203\\\\t`references/video-candidate-audit.md` before calling it. Use\\\\n   204\\\\t`list_doc_segments(mode=select)` in the same way for document coverage gaps.\\\\n   205\\\\tFor an Answer Plan whose `coverage_requirement=full_asset`, read\\\\n   206\\\\t`references/full-asset-coverage.md` before catalog traversal and collection updates.\\\\n   207\\\\tEstablish the catalog, review all bounded pages, and inspect retained/uncertain\\\\n   208\\\\tcandidates. Neither search hits nor a fully paged catalog proves a source-wide total.\\\\n   209\\\\t\\\\n   210\\\\t### Phase 4: Evidence Verification\\\\n   211\\\\t\\\\n   212\\\\tInspect evidence by the information type needed for the fact, not by the\\\\n   213\\\\tcandidate container type. Use inspect tools only after candidate evidence has\\\\n   214\\\\tbeen selected from `knowledge_search`, `list_video_segments`, or\\\\n   215\\\\t`list_doc_segments`.\\\\n   216\\\\t\\\\n   217\\\\tFor video evidence, pass the selected `evidence_id` and an evidence-backed\\\\n   218\\\\t`frame_time`. If a reliable frame image or user-provided time already answers\\\\n   219\\\\tthe requested temporal scope, use it directly. Otherwise, use `video_inspect_2_0`\\\\n   220\\\\tto locate a suitable frame; its numeric claims locate the moment but do not\\\\n   221\\\\tclose the visual grounding slot. If no frame can represent the requested temporal\\\\n   222\\\\tmeaning with a distinguishable target, keep the slot unverified and state the\\\\n   223\\\\tevidence limitation instead of inferring a count.\\\\n   224\\\\t\\\\n   225\\\\tPass a focused query that identifies and distinguishes the intended target;\\\\n   226\\\\tthe `visual-ground` skill defines that tool-specific request format.\\\\n   227\\\\tInspect `keep_for_inspect` candidates for each uncovered answer slot before\\\\n   228\\\\tbroadening retrieval. An eligible inspect claim is evidence for your assessment,\\\\n   229\\\\tnot an automatic declaration that a goal is complete.\\\\n   230\\\\tMark it `verified` only when its required evidence scope has an eligible inspect\\\\n   231\\\\tclaim; evidence outside that scope may inform retrieval but cannot close it.\\\\n   232\\\\tAfter a failed, empty, or ineligible inspect result, the slot remains unverified.\\\\n   233\\\\tInspect the next kept candidate; keep the slot `pending` with a note when existing\\\\n   234\\\\tcandidates cannot cover it, then retrieve more if appropriate.\\\\n   235\\\\t\\\\n   236\\\\tAfter a meaningful change in evidence or investigation direction, update the plan\\\\n   237\\\\twith your conclusion and remaining gap. Routine tool calls need no separate plan update.\\\\n   238\\\\tBefore final synthesis, use `answer_plan(action=review)` to assess each current goal\\\\n   239\\\\tagainst supporting and conflicting evidence: what interpretation was retained or\\\\n   240\\\\tchanged, what checks resolved the doubt, and what remains uncertain. Check the\\\\n   241\\\\toriginal question for omitted or reinterpreted requirements, not just completion of the plan.\\\\n   242\\\\tFor multiple verified facts that could answer one requested quantity, record their\\\\n   243\\\\trelationship in the assessment before choosing the answer: repeated support for the\\\\n   244\\\\tsame fact, non-overlapping parts of one requested whole, alternative scopes, or\\\\n   245\\\\tindependent facts. Treat them as parts of a total only when their metric, period and\\\\n   246\\\\tunit match, their scopes do not overlap, and the original question asks for the\\\\n   247\\\\tcombined scope. Otherwise give the scoped values separately or record the remaining\\\\n   248\\\\tinterpretation in `uncertainties`; do not choose one by an unstated convention.\\\\n   249\\\\tAn unqualified metric asks for its overall value within the stated subject and\\\\n   250\\\\tperiod. If the source reports that metric only as non-overlapping components whose\\\\n   251\\\\tscopes together cover that request, use their combined value as the direct answer\\\\n   252\\\\tand show the inputs. Do not turn source section labels into alternative user\\\\n   253\\\\tinterpretations unless the wording or evidence makes those scopes mutually\\\\n   254\\\\texclusive.\\\\n   255\\\\tFor each unresolved gap, state its effect on the conclusion: partial findings do not establish\\\\n   256\\\\ta total or absence. Review takes `items` and `original_question_check`,\\\\n   257\\\\trequired `uncertainties`, and optional `limitations`; use an empty uncertainty list\\\\n   258\\\\tonly after checking that no materially different supported interpretation remains.\\\\n   259\\\\tIn the same review, set `conclusion=answer_supported` only when evidence supports a substantive\\\\n   260\\\\tanswer to the requested fact, including a supported partial answer with clear limits. Set\\\\n   261\\\\t`conclusion=requested_fact_unanswerable` when the requested fact cannot be determined; related,\\\\n   262\\\\tconditional or possible answers do not make it answered. Record the evidence basis in the required\\\\n   263\\\\t`conclusion_reason`.\\\\n   264\\\\tThe runtime owns version tracking, so no revision is needed.\\\\n   265\\\\tUse `view` when you need current evidence. A recorded review is your assessment, not an independent correctness verdict;\\\\n   266\\\\tthe final answer must use the evidence citations that support its actual statements.\\\\n   267\\\\tDo not calculate merely because\\\\n   268\\\\tone input was found; every required input slot must be verified or explicitly\\\\n   269\\\\tnot found.\\\\n   270\\\\t\\\\n   271\\\\tFor collections, define answer_unit and record distinct inspect-supported\\\\n   272\\\\tverified_items, not chunks or citations. Read `references/full-asset-coverage.md`\\\\n   273\\\\tbefore recording collection identities, grouped quantities or full-source completion.\\\\n   274\\\\t\\\\n   275\\\\tFor numeric calculations, bind every input to a verified value and supporting claim.\\\\n   276\\\\tOnce every input is verified, read `references/sandbox-computation-rules.md` and\\\\n   277\\\\tuse DeepAgents `execute` for the calculation.\\\\n   278\\\\tDo not calculate from values that exist only in search or catalog output.\\\\n   279\\\\tCount deduplicated answer units, not chunks, hits, citations or inspect calls.\\\\n   280\\\\t\\\\n   281\\\\t### Visual Grounding And Time Scope\\\\n   282\\\\t\\\\n   283\\\\t- Match the evidence scope to the requested fact. A frame-local count or location\\\\n   284\\\\t  requires a current-run `visual_ground` claim on a reliable frame time. When a\\\\n   285\\\\t  reliable frame is already supplied by evidence or the user, do not require an\\\\n   286\\\\t  extra video inspection merely to recover that same timestamp.\\\\n   287\\\\t- A source-wide count concerns events or items across the selected video or\\\\n   288\\\\t  document. One frame cannot prove a source-wide total; establish catalog\\\\n   289\\\\t  coverage, inspect retained candidates, and deduplicate answer units.\\\\n   290\\\\t- For duration, verify the semantic start and end boundaries with eligible\\\\n   291\\\\t  inspect claims. Catalog summaries are locator hints, not proof of the duration.\\\\n   292\\\\t- Classify counting requests as frame-local objects, repeated actions, global text\\\\n   293\\\\t  occurrences, duration or parameter, or global categories. A single frame cannot\\\\n   294\\\\t  establish an across-time total. For cumulative occurrences, audit the bounded\\\\n   295\\\\t  catalog, inspect plausible occurrences, and expand coverage before answering zero.\\\\n   296\\\\t- For continuing actions, use a verified final-state frame for visible-object\\\\n   297\\\\t  counting. Confirm that the frame, object alias, and requested temporal scope\\\\n   298\\\\t  match before answering.\\\\n   299\\\\t\\\\n   300\\\\t### Phase 5: Answer\\\\n   301\\\\t\\\\n   302\\\\tUse verified claims, valid historical verified claims, or `uploaded_image_search`\\\\n   303\\\\twith `answer_from_image`. Cite each knowledge-base factual claim with its exact\\\\n   304\\\\treturned token. Without eligible evidence, state insufficiency.\\\\n   305\\\\tEach evidence-dependent slot must be verified or have a concrete uncovered\\\\n   306\\\\treason; plausible candidates awaiting inspection or rejection mean it is not ready.\\\\n   307\\\\tAnswers only stating insufficiency, library metadata, or no knowledge-base facts\\\\n   308\\\\tneed no citation.\\\\n   309\\\\t\\\\n   310\\\\t## Tool Ordering Rules\\\\n   311\\\\t\\\\n   312\\\\tThese are partial-order constraints, not a mandatory full sequence.\\\\n   313\\\\t\\\\n   314\\\\t- For a relevant user upload, use `uploaded_image_search`, not `read_file`,\\\\n   315\\\\t  before knowledge retrieval or inspection.\\\\n   316\\\\t- Call `document_inspect` only after `knowledge_search` has returned selected document\\\\n   317\\\\t  evidence. It reviews the full source page; do not use it for user-uploaded workspace images.\\\\n   318\\\\t- For selected video evidence, `visual_ground.frame_time` must come from a\\\\n   319\\\\t  reliable frame image, `video_inspect_2_0`, or user-provided timing; never invent\\\\n   320\\\\t  a timestamp without a visual basis.\\\\n   321\\\\t\\\\n   322\\\\t## Reference Loading\\\\n   323\\\\t\\\\n   324\\\\t- `references/answer-plan.md`: goal replacement, retrieval bindings and plan payload details.\\\\n   325\\\\t- `references/full-asset-coverage.md`: full-source catalog traversal and collection bookkeeping.\\\\n   326\\\\t\\\\n   327\\\\tRead references only when the matching condition applies:\\\\n   328\\\\t\\\\n   329\\\\t- `references/inspect-results.md`: inspect result eligibility.\\\\n   330\\\\t- `references/evidence-candidate-audit.md`: ambiguous, multi-candidate,\\\\n   331\\\\t  cross-modal, or coverage-expansion candidate selection.\\\\n   332\\\\t- `references/generation-guidelines.md`: specialized comparison, workflow or other output templates.\\\\n   333\\\\t- `references/evidence-modality-policy.md`: multimodal evidence conflicts.\\\\n   334\\\\t- `references/video-candidate-audit.md`: video-specific chunk and temporal\\\\n   335\\\\t  coverage selection.\\\\n   336\\\\t- `references/claim-reconciliation.md`: same-fact claim merging/conflicts.\\\\n   337\\\\t- `references/citation-rules.md`: citation eligibility or formatting details beyond the rules below.\\\\n   338\\\\t- `references/sandbox-computation-rules.md`: exact calculation with `execute`.\\\\n   339\\\\t\\\\n   340\\\\t## Tool Capability Boundaries\\\\n   341\\\\t\\\\n   342\\\\t- `uploaded_image_search` analyzes one user-uploaded image before text query\\\\n   343\\\\t  refinement. Use it only for workspace uploads, not for image Evidence returned\\\\n   344\\\\t  by `knowledge_search`.\\\\n   345\\\\t- `video_inspect_2_0` extracts traceable claims from one selected video\\\\n   346\\\\t  evidence range. It may adapt frame resolution, crop a relevant region, or\\\\n   347\\\\t  increase sampling around an uncertain moment. It does not transcribe speech,\\\\n   348\\\\t  verify exact audio wording, search other ranges, or combine multiple clips.\\\\n   349\\\\t- visual_ground verifies object counts and spatial grounding from images or\\\\n   350\\\\t  sampled video frames. For video, it samples the selected evidence time range\\\\n   351\\\\t  and returns inspect-style claims. It does not search for candidate evidence and\\\\n   352\\\\t  does not replace `video_inspect_2_0`.\\\\n   353\\\\t- For speech, dialogue, reassurance, reminders, announcements, or audio\\\\n   354\\\\t  instructions, use indexed transcript snippets only as locator hints. If no\\\\n   355\\\\t  enabled inspect tool can verify the fact as a claim, state that evidence is\\\\n   356\\\\t  insufficient.\\\\n   357\\\\t- For visible text in media, use visual text snippets only as locator hints.\\\\n   358\\\\t  Verify only what an enabled inspect tool can read as a claim; otherwise state\\\\n   359\\\\t  that evidence is insufficient.\\\\n   360\\\\t- For document/SOP text, tables, figures, and charts, call `document_inspect` on\\\\n   361\\\\t  evidence copied from `knowledge_search` or a segment locator returned by\\\\n   362\\\\t  `list_doc_segments(mode=select)`. It resolves the page context before inspection.\\\\n   363\\\\t\\\\n   364\\\\t## Video Evidence Calling Policy\\\\n   365\\\\t\\\\n   366\\\\tBefore video inspection, read `references/video-candidate-audit.md` for copied locator\\\\n   367\\\\tboundaries, sampling defaults, candidate budgets and justified repeat calls.\\\\n   368\\\\tThe main Agent reconciles claims across ranges; do not invent locator boundaries.\\\\n   369\\\\t\\\\n   370\\\\t## Primary Evidence Modality\\\\n   371\\\\t\\\\n   372\\\\tChoose the primary evidence modality by the fact being verified:\\\\n   373\\\\t\\\\n   374\\\\t- Visible action, count, posture, object state, or scene content -> video.\\\\n   375\\\\t- Visible written text, labels, signs, panels, or screen content -> image/video\\\\n   376\\\\t  only when the enabled inspect tool can read it reliably.\\\\n   377\\\\t- Document/SOP rules, parameters, or written procedure text -> text.\\\\n   378\\\\t\\\\n   379\\\\tIf modalities conflict, prefer the primary modality for that fact. Use other\\\\n   380\\\\tmodalities as context or locator evidence only. When unsure, see\\\\n   381\\\\t`references/evidence-modality-policy.md`.\\\\n   382\\\\t\\\\n   383\\\\t## Claim Reconciliation\\\\n   384\\\\t\\\\n   385\\\\tBefore treating claims as conflicting, decide whether they assert the same fact\\\\n   386\\\\tunder the same modality scope. A visual absence claim limits what was visible in\\\\n   387\\\\tframe; it does not negate speech evidence from the same time range. If claims\\\\n   388\\\\tanswer different scopes, combine them with explicit boundaries. If they conflict\\\\n   389\\\\ton the same fact and scope, prefer the primary evidence modality for that fact or\\\\n   390\\\\tstate that evidence conflicts. See `references/claim-reconciliation.md`.\\\\n   391\\\\t\\\\n   392\\\\t## Historical Claims\\\\n   393\\\\t\\\\n   394\\\\tHistorical verified claims may be used only to restate or summarize the same\\\\n   395\\\\tfact. Copy their stable `citation_token` exactly. If the user asks about a new\\\\n   396\\\\tstate, count, later time point, action result, or uncovered property, call the\\\\n   397\\\\tcorresponding inspect tool again.\\\\n   398\\\\t\\\\n   399\\\\t## Final Answer Generation\\\\n   400\\\\t\\\\n   401\\\\tUse the final plan review to check the original question's scope, omissions,\\\\n   402\\\\tadditional matching items and conflicts. Revise the plan or state unresolved limits.\\\\n   403\\\\t\\\\n   404\\\\t- Keep original terminology, part numbers, protocol names, document titles and\\\\n   405\\\\t  standard abbreviations.\\\\n   406\\\\t- Put the final user-facing answer in a message with no tool calls; finish any\\\\n   407\\\\t  housekeeping tools in an earlier turn.\\\\n   408\\\\t- Answer from verified claims; express unresolved scope in the conclusion itself,\\\\n   409\\\\t  not as a disclaimer after an unsupported total. Partial answers or clarification are valid.\\\\n   410\\\\t- Preserve source units, currency and scale unless the user requests conversion.\\\\n   411\\\\t  If calculation requires unit normalization, explain the conversion and label the result's unit.\\\\n   412\\\\t- Answer only the output requested by the user. Do not append document-wide\\\\n   413\\\\t  background, related-item lists, or other verified facts that do not answer an\\\\n   414\\\\t  explicit answer slot.\\\\n   415\\\\t- Do not write tool display_label, timestamps, segment IDs, or source ranges in\\\\n   416\\\\t  answer text. The citation renderer resolves those details from citation tokens.\\\\n   417\\\\t- Do not present raw tool metadata, chunk ids, file paths, or internal evidence\\\\n   418\\\\t  ids as user-facing source labels.\\\\n   419\\\\t- Do not narrate searches, inspections, plan updates, or tool failures unless a\\\\n   420\\\\t  concrete evidence limitation changes the answer; then state only that\\\\n   421\\\\t  user-relevant limitation.\\\\n   422\\\\t- Write the complete user-facing answer once, then stop; do not append a second\\\\n   423\\\\t  summary or restatement of the same answer.\\\\n   424\\\\t- If you need to correct the answer, rewrite that same answer in place; do not\\\\n   425\\\\t  append a separate summary after a finished answer.\\\\n   426\\\\t\\\\n   427\\\\t## Citation Rules\\\\n   428\\\\t\\\\n   429\\\\t- Use exact current-run `agent_citation` tokens returned by tools: `[1]`, `[2]`.\\\\n   430\\\\t- Never merge tokens. Write `[3][4][5]`, not `[3-5]`.\\\\n   431\\\\t- For more examples, see `references/citation-rules.md`.\\\", \\\"additional_kwargs\\\": {}, \\\"response_metadata\\\": {}, \\\"type\\\": \\\"tool\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"read_file\\\", \\\"id\\\": \\\"36d72298-5834-460f-8c1b-fd86b07c4cf7\\\", \\\"tool_call_id\\\": \\\"chatcmpl-tool-bce25656b6cae8c4\\\", \\\"artifact\\\": null, \\\"status\\\": \\\"success\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"additional_kwargs\\\": {}, \\\"response_metadata\\\": {\\\"finish_reason\\\": \\\"tool_calls\\\", \\\"model_name\\\": \\\"viknow-agent-chat\\\", \\\"model_provider\\\": \\\"openai\\\"}, \\\"type\\\": \\\"ai\\\", \\\"name\\\": null, \\\"id\\\": \\\"lc_run--01a0bc69-82bd-73b3-92d0-e4abc4a71858\\\", \\\"tool_calls\\\": [{\\\"name\\\": \\\"knowledge_discover\\\", \\\"args\\\": {\\\"query\\\": \\\"上海唯纳新思资源交付通知书 PDF\\\"}, \\\"id\\\": \\\"chatcmpl-tool-81d3ef4a0b04384